< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"status","title":"Logic Pro status","description":"Whether Kumi's bridge in Logic Pro is connected: the Logic Pro and bridge versions, the open project, and whether Logic Pro is busy (a dialog, a render). With several Logic Pro instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"discover","title":"Find running Logic Pro","description":"Every running Logic Pro with Kumi's bridge: process id, port, resource folder, versions, open project, and whether it answers. Use it when status reports none, or to choose among several.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"read","title":"Read Logic Pro","description":"Rows of one kind from the open Logic Pro project, a page at a time: {items, nextCursor?, epoch}. Pass parent (a row's ref) to read what is inside it, such as a track's regions, plug-ins, sends, Smart Controls or automation, or a plug-in's parameters; pass the previous page's nextCursor as cursor for the next page. Or pass ref alone for the one object it names. Refs hold until the epoch changes. With several Logic Pro instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["project","track","region","note","plugin","send","marker","tempo","param","smart","automation","recent"],"description":"What to read in Logic Pro."},"parent":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the rows are in: a track for its regions, plug-ins, sends, Smart Controls or automation; an output strip (the Stereo Out is <epoch>:output:1) for its plug-ins; a plug-in for its parameters; a region for its notes. Notes, parameters, Smart Controls and automation need theirs."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of one object to read instead of a page of rows."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page (50 by default)."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"snapshot","title":"Logic Pro snapshot","description":"The open Logic Pro project on one screen: {epoch, project, transport, tracks, selection, markers?}. What is too big to include is named under truncated, to read with `read`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"rows":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["project","track","region","plugin","send","marker","tempo"]},"description":"The kinds to read whole instead of the one screen: the answer is {epoch, rows: {kind: [rows]}, totals: {kind: n}, truncated?: [kinds]}, each kind's rows exactly what read pages for it, in one epoch."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10000,"description":"With rows: the most rows of a kind (10000 by default); a kind with more is named under truncated, to page with read."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus","title":"Logic Pro focus","description":"What the producer is looking at in Logic Pro: {epoch, view, selection, transport, changed}. Cheap enough to poll about every 150 ms; read again only when changed moves.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus_body","title":"Logic Pro view","description":"What Logic Pro shows in one of its views, ready to draw: pass kind, and ref (the track or region it is about) or window (the range to show) where the kind takes them. Long ones come in pages: pass the nextCursor as cursor.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["tree","notes","timeline","routing"],"description":"Which view."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the view is about: a track for tree and routing, a region for notes (the selected one when left out)."},"around":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of a track to centre the first page of the timeline's lanes on: the page starts half a page above it, and says where in `from`."},"window":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"number"},"to":{"type":"number"}},"required":["from","to"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The range of the timeline to show, in beats from the project's start."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page."}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_preview","title":"Preview a Logic Pro change","description":"What one change would do in Logic Pro, without making it: {transactionId, confirmation, prior, display, target, epoch}. Apply it with change_apply.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","description":"The change kind."},"input":{"type":"object","description":"What the kind takes."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs in input came from."}},"required":["kind","input"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_apply","title":"Apply a Logic Pro change","description":"Makes a previewed change in Logic Pro, as one named step of Logic Pro's undo. The same idempotencyKey again returns the first answer and changes nothing. state is applied, or uncertain when Logic Pro didn't answer.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"type":"string","description":"The confirmation change_preview gave."},"idempotencyKey":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string","description":"The change's name in Logic Pro's undo history."}},"required":["transactionId","confirmation","idempotencyKey"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_undo","title":"Undo a Logic Pro change","description":"Takes a change back as a new named step in Logic Pro: exactly what it changed is put back. Refused (code changed) if those values changed since, unless discard.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"const":"undo"},"idempotencyKey":{"type":"string"},"discard":{"type":"boolean","description":"Put the values back even if they changed since."}},"required":["transactionId","confirmation","idempotencyKey"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"transport_stop","title":"Stop Logic Pro","description":"Stops Logic Pro's playback and recording at once.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"transport_play","title":"Play Logic Pro","description":"Starts Logic Pro's playback from where the playhead is (cursor_set moves it first).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"cursor_set","title":"Move Logic Pro's cursor","description":"Moves Logic Pro's edit cursor to positionBeats (quarter notes from the start) or position (seconds); the play position follows while it plays.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"positionBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"position":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"undo_step_begin","title":"Begin one Logic Pro undo step","description":"Opens one step of Logic Pro's undo around the changes that follow, where Logic Pro gives one: {stepId}. Close it with undo_step_end.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"undo_step_end","title":"End the Logic Pro undo step","description":"Closes the step undo_step_begin opened; label names it in Logic Pro's undo by what it did.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"stepId":{"type":"string"},"label":{"type":"string","maxLength":200}},"required":["stepId"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_release","title":"Forget changes","description":"Changes that won't be undone any more: the host forgets them (at most 64 at a time).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionIds":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":64}},"required":["transactionIds"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"project_save","title":"Save the Logic Pro project","description":"Saves the open Logic Pro project where it is (File > Save), or as path (a whole path to a .logicx package that isn't there yet; the project is that file from then on). A project never saved is saved only under path, and never over a file. (version is REAPER's: Logic Pro refuses it.)","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"version":{"type":"boolean"},"path":{"type":"string"},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the project was read in: if the project open now is another, the save is refused as stale."}},"required":["epoch"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"bounce","title":"Bounce the Logic Pro project","description":"Bounces the open Logic Pro project from startBeats to endBeats (beats from the project's start) to an audio file at path, a whole path to a file that isn't there yet (.wav, or .aif for aiff24), in a folder that is (File > Bounce > Project or Section: Uncompressed in format, wav24 by default, Normalize off): what Logic Pro plays, through the Stereo Out. The file is found on disk and its header read: the answer gives bounced (its path), format, bytes, seconds, rate, channels and bits. A file written, not the project: no change and no undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"startBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"endBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"path":{"type":"string"},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["wav24","wav16","wav32f","aiff24"]},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the project was read in: if the project open now is another, it is refused as stale."}},"required":["startBeats","endBeats","path","epoch"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"export_tracks","title":"Export Logic Pro's tracks as audio files","description":"Exports every track of the open Logic Pro project as an audio file of its own into the folder path, whole and there already (File > Export > All Tracks as Audio Files, with the options the producer set in Logic Pro): the answer lists the files Logic Pro wrote there (name, bytes, seconds). Files written, not the project: no change and no undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"path":{"type":"string"},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the project was read in: if the project open now is another, it is refused as stale."}},"required":["path","epoch"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"hear","title":"Hear a part of the Logic Pro project","description":"Plays a part of the open Logic Pro project and captures what Logic Pro outputs, after the Stereo Out, into a WAV file in folder (32-bit float at the output device's rate): the cycle and the metronome off, the playhead placed exactly on the part's first beat, Logic played and followed past the part's end, the capture cut to the part; then Logic Pro put back as it was (its playhead, solos, metronome and cycle). solo hears those tracks alone (none: the whole mix, no track soloed); a track the producer muted stays silent, and the note says so. The answer: file, seconds, sampleRate, channels, lead (0: the file starts on the part's first beat), peak and rms (of full scale, 1.0), aligned (by, latencyMs, errorMs: how the capture was cut to the beats), fromBeats, beats, mute, solo, metronome, epoch, note, and notPutBack (what of Logic Pro couldn't be put back). busy while Logic Pro plays or a dialog is up. The call lasts as long as the part plays, plus a margin. A file written, not the project: no change and no undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"fromBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"description":"Where the part starts, in beats from the project's start."},"beats":{"type":"number","minimum":0.25,"maximum":14400,"description":"How long the part is, in beats (a pass plays at most 600 s)."},"folder":{"type":"string","description":"A whole path to a folder that is there: the files go into it, named by the bridge (kumi-hear-<n>.wav, kumi-audition-<n>-<k>.wav, kumi-render-<n>.wav), never over a file."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs were read in, when the request gives one: if the project's is another, it is refused as stale."},"mute":{"type":"boolean","description":"Logic Pro is kept from the speakers while it is captured (false by default: the producer hears it)."},"solo":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":64,"description":"Tracks (their refs) heard alone, soloed for the pass; none for the whole mix."}},"required":["fromBeats","beats","folder"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"audition","title":"Audition candidates in Logic Pro","description":"Hears each candidate over the same part of the open Logic Pro project, one pass after the other in their order and in one capture, each as hear hears it: a track ({\"ref\": …}) soloed alone, or the whole mix ({\"mix\": true}); Logic Pro is put back as it was after the last. The answer: candidates, in their order, each its candidate (ref, or mix), its name, and what hear's file holds (file, seconds, sampleRate, channels, lead, peak, rms, note); then aligned, fromBeats, beats, mute, metronome, epoch and notPutBack. The call lasts each pass's part plus a margin. Files written, not the project: no change and no undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"fromBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"description":"Where the part starts, in beats from the project's start."},"beats":{"type":"number","minimum":0.25,"maximum":14400,"description":"How long the part is, in beats (a pass plays at most 600 s)."},"folder":{"type":"string","description":"A whole path to a folder that is there: the files go into it, named by the bridge (kumi-hear-<n>.wav, kumi-audition-<n>-<k>.wav, kumi-render-<n>.wav), never over a file."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs were read in, when the request gives one: if the project's is another, it is refused as stale."},"mute":{"type":"boolean","description":"Logic Pro is kept from the speakers while it is captured (false by default: the producer hears it)."},"candidates":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":16,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"ref":{"type":"string","description":"A track, heard soloed alone."},"mix":{"type":"boolean","description":"true: the whole mix."}},"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidates","fromBeats","beats","folder"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"render","title":"Render a part of the Logic Pro project","description":"Bounces a part of the open Logic Pro project offline into a WAV file in folder (File > Bounce over the part: 32-bit float at the project's rate, Normalize off, the metronome off; nothing plays): ref, a track, is soloed alone for it, so its audio passes its plug-ins and the Stereo Out's (the note says so); without ref, the whole mix. The solos and the metronome are put back. The answer: file, seconds, sampleRate, channels, bits, lead (0), fromBeats, beats, metronome, epoch, ref, note and notPutBack. A file written, not the project: no change and no undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"fromBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"description":"Where the part starts, in beats from the project's start."},"beats":{"type":"number","minimum":0.25,"maximum":14400,"description":"How long the part is, in beats (a pass plays at most 600 s)."},"folder":{"type":"string","description":"A whole path to a folder that is there: the files go into it, named by the bridge (kumi-hear-<n>.wav, kumi-audition-<n>-<k>.wav, kumi-render-<n>.wav), never over a file."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs were read in, when the request gives one: if the project's is another, it is refused as stale."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"A track to bounce alone, soloed for it; left out, the whole mix."}},"required":["fromBeats","beats","folder"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}}]}}
